{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres","id":1501067,"title":"Did victorian mage use minor spheres?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-22T15:02:03-08:00","id":1501067,"title":"Did victorian mage use minor spheres?","content":"I heard it was supposed to and that it used the majors instead. if so I feel betrayed! LOL<br /> <br /> I was really hoping for canon minor spheres presented by serious authors. <br /> <br /> PS I just found out it was released, haven't used the internet in a while, lol, like several months with no smart phone and no laptop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T17:13:12-08:00","id":1501078,"title":"","content":"Only if you want them to.<br /> <br /> Seriously though, minor Spheres have been around a long time. It makes sense that the Victorians would have both known of and used the minor Spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T20:08:23-08:00","id":1501095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres#post1501067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard it was supposed to and that it used the majors instead. if so I feel betrayed! LOL<br /> <br /> I was really hoping for canon minor spheres presented by serious authors.<br /> <br /> PS I just found out it was released, haven't used the internet in a while, lol, like several months with no smart phone and no laptop.</div> </div> </div> </div>it wasn\u2019t \u201csupposed to\u201d. There was a pitch for a Victorian Mage book floating around the internet for decades that proposed doing that, but this book was never that proposal greenlit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T07:58:17-08:00","id":1501135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1501078#post1501078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if you want them to.<br /> <br /> Seriously though, minor Spheres have been around a long time. It makes sense that the Victorians would have both known of and used the minor Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Officially? No. Minor Spheres have only appeared once in an official Mage book (the Revised Storyteller's Handbook); and that was a book of optional and variant rules for Storytellers. <br /> <br /> Mind you, I very much like the concept of Minor Spheres; and I bought the STV supplement about them right away. But they haven't \u201cbeen around a long time\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T08:53:05-08:00","id":1501142,"title":"","content":"Not to make us all feel old or anything, but the ST Handbook came out over 20 years ago... the minor Spheres might not have been a big thing in the original run of the game and all, but product that will turn 21 later this year has had plenty of time to work its way into stuff that counts as been around for awhile now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T09:36:38-08:00","id":1501144,"title":"","content":"Oh, it's been around; just not as something that's part of the setting. It was an option, no different in that regard from the Echoes alternative system of Paradox and Resonance (pp.22\u201326) or the Transmogrification option (pp.28\u201329), or even A World Without Spheres (p.30). The whole book was about \u201cThe Golden Rule\u201d: if the rules are getting in the way of the game, change the rules.<br /> <br /> I say this because Astromancer's post implied that Minor Spheres have been <i>part of the setting</i> for a long time (\u201cIt makes sense that the Victorians would have both known of and used the minor Spheres\u201d); but they have <i>never</i> been part of the setting. They have only ever existed as a rules option. While there was a pitch for a Victorian Mage game that would have made them official, that never happened; and more generally, I know of no instances other than the Storyteller's Handbook and the Book of Fragments (a STV supplement) that even mentions them.<br /> <br /> Again, I like the Minor Spheres, both for their conceptual implications (that there are Other Ways to Do Things, and that the Nine Spheres aren't necessarily hard-coded into reality) and for the practical implications (Minor Spheres have the potential to make things easier in narrow areas than the Nine Spheres allow, such as allowing things to be done with a single Sphere that would normally be split up among multiple Spheres). But the issue here isn't whether or not I like them; it's whether or not they're part of the default setting. And (from my perspective, sadly), they're not and never have been.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T21:13:42-08:00","id":1501208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1501135#post1501135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Officially? No. Minor Spheres have only appeared once in an official Mage book (the Revised Storyteller's Handbook); and that was a book of optional and variant rules for Storytellers.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I very much like the concept of Minor Spheres; and I bought the STV supplement about them right away. But they haven't \u201cbeen around a long time\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you rate it for the ten bucks cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T21:18:08-08:00","id":1501209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1501144#post1501144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the issue here isn't whether or not I like them; it's whether or not they're part of the default setting. And (from my perspective, sadly), they're not and never have been.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>very good point I agree. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T21:40:53-08:00","id":1501210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres#post1501067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard it was supposed to</div> </div> </div> </div>As others have noted: not really.<br /> <br /> Back around 2006 I made an outline for a Victorian Mage as a fan project, because (at the time) it was unlikely we'd ever see an official Mage: The Ascension project again. That outline included Minor Spheres. <br /> <br /> I wanted to use Minor Spheres as sort of a halfway point between the Pillars of Dark Ages: Mage and the full spheres of modern Mage, as an indication that the Traditions were more insular and focusing on their own magics rather than collaborating: the focus was on individual Traditions (and factions within those Traditions), less a cohesive Council of Nine.<br /> <br /> When VicMage was added to the schedule after Mage20 came out in 2014ish, we used my old outline as a placeholder. It's ultimately not the outline we finally went with. The new outline had a different story with different moods and themes. It was a better outline and ultimately led to a stronger game than what I came up with as a fan a decade earlier. It would have been nice to incorporate Minor Spheres, but in the end there wasn't a particularly good reason for their inclusion this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 01-24-2023, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T22:11:06-08:00","id":1501211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1501208#post1501208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would you rate it for the ten bucks cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth the price. Three chapters: the first deals with the theory behind Minor Spheres; the second provides write-ups for nine sample Minor Spheres (Desire, Emergence, Fire, Glory, Harmony, Hearth, Meaning, Metamorphosis, and Night); and the third chapter provides guidelines for making your own Minor Spheres and how to run a game that has Minor Spheres <i>instead of</i> the Major Spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T10:18:41-08:00","id":1501246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1501210#post1501210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to use Minor Spheres as sort of a halfway point between the Pillars of Dark Ages: Mage and the full spheres of modern Mage, as an indication that the Traditions were more insular and focusing on their own magics rather than collaborating: the focus was on individual Traditions (and factions within those Traditions), less a cohesive Council of Nine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really love this idea. I'd hate to ask but do you have any of those notes that survived or could be shared? I understand if you don't/can't.\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T10:28:40-08:00","id":1501247,"title":"","content":"What I just wrote was basically as far as the notes went. &quot;Maybe we should do this. Let's figure something out.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T10:39:54-08:00","id":1501248,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, the idea works better for the Disparates, Alliance or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T04:22:18-08:00","id":1504746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1501211#post1501211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth the price. Three chapters: the first deals with the theory behind Minor Spheres; the second provides write-ups for nine sample Minor Spheres (Desire, Emergence, Fire, Glory, Harmony, Hearth, Meaning, Metamorphosis, and Night); and the third chapter provides guidelines for making your own Minor Spheres and how to run a game that has Minor Spheres <i>instead of</i> the Major Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the minor Spheres thing has been implemented in the forms of the pillars. The only difference is that pillars are more, uhm, heavy,. than minor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T07:06:05-08:00","id":1504751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1504746#post1504746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, the minor Spheres thing has been implemented in the forms of the pillars. The only difference is that pillars are more, uhm, heavy,. than minor</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pillars method of portraying and describing Magick Effects in M:tA also has the Foundation as an important mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T07:18:09-08:00","id":1504754,"title":"","content":"<b>The Book of Fragments</b> makes a point that Minor Spheres aren't Pillars. What they have in common is that they generally \u201ccut across\u201d the Major Spheres (although the Hermetic Forma and the Batini \u201cAl-Hajj\u201d line up rather closely with modern Spheres, though still not perfectly); but Pillars are at once <i>broader than</i> Major Spheres and <i>more restricted</i>: a Hermetic in the Dark Ages could use Corona/Primus spells to access the Astral Umbra and command its denizens, something that Mind/Prime cannot do; <i>and </i>they could use Corona to do everything that a modern student of Mind can do; but at the same time, Primus could <i>only</i> be used by the Order of Hermes: the Hermetic Focus was baked into them, to the point that each Fellowship had its own Foundation, and learning Pillars that had been developed by other Fellowships required learning their Foundations, too. <br /> <br /> By contrast, Minor Spheres are more limited than Major Spheres; it's the reason why they have lower experience point costs. But they're also not tied to specific Foci (in the M20 sense of the term).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T07:43:16-08:00","id":1504758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1504754#post1504754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Book of Fragments</b> makes a point that Minor Spheres aren't Pillars. What they have in common is that they generally \u201ccut across\u201d the Major Spheres (although the Hermetic Forma and the Batini \u201cAl-Hajj\u201d line up rather closely with modern Spheres, though still not perfectly); but Pillars are at once <i>broader than</i> Major Spheres and <i>more restricted</i>: a Hermetic in the Dark Ages could use Corona/Primus spells to access the Astral Umbra and command its denizens, something that Mind/Prime cannot do; <i>and </i>they could use Corona to do everything that a modern student of Mind can do; but at the same time, Primus could <i>only</i> be used by the Order of Hermes: the Hermetic Focus was baked into them, to the point that each Fellowship had its own Foundation, and learning Pillars that had been developed by other Fellowships required learning their Foundations, too.<br /> <br /> By contrast, Minor Spheres are more limited than Major Spheres; it's the reason why they have lower experience point costs. But they're also not tied to specific Foci (in the M20 sense of the term).</div> </div> </div> </div>Lower experience costs? Strange, i thought the St handbook gave them &quot;current rating x 8&quot; just as usual<br /> <br /> Did this book of Fragments change it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T08:00:01-08:00","id":1504760,"title":"","content":"Yes, it did. It essentially takes the <i>concept </i>of Minor Spheres, but completely changes the <i>mechanics</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T08:38:09-08:00","id":1504762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1501210#post1501210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As others have noted: not really.<br /> <br /> Back around 2006 I made an outline for a Victorian Mage as a fan project, because (at the time) it was unlikely we'd ever see an official Mage: The Ascension project again. That outline included Minor Spheres.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>it must've have been a wonderful feeling,to be able to it officially","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T02:28:37-08:00","id":1504826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1504760#post1504760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it did. It essentially takes the <i>concept </i>of Minor Spheres, but completely changes the <i>mechanics</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you remember how much xp it costs? <br /> I actually consider adopting the concept for dark ages mage <br /> A minor pillar, so to speak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T06:24:47-08:00","id":1504840,"title":"","content":"5xp for the first dot, and current level times four for each dot after that. At character creation, Minor Spheres cost four freebie points per dot. However, there's also the restriction that before you can buy that first dot, you must first put two dots into the \u201cadjacent Major Spheres\u201d. <br /> <br /> <b>Foreign Magicks</b>, another STV supplement that features Minors Spheres (for crossover purposes), replaces this requirement with the requirement to take an appropriate Merit first: the Ghoul Merit gives you access to the Minor Spheres of Blood, Immortality, and Dominance; the Kinfolk Merit gives you access to the Minor Spheres of Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm; the Medium Merit gives access to the Minor Spheres of Necromancy, Oblivion, and Passion; and the Kinain Merit gives access to the Minor Spheres of Dreams, Names, and Oaths.<br /> <br /> (<b>Foreign Magicks</b> takes as its premise the idea that an Awakened Ghoul, for example, gets these Minor Spheres <i>instead of </i>developing Disciplines, and that a Kinain mage uses Dreams to perceive chimera instead of that being an innate benefit of the Kinain Merit. In short, these Merits are reimagined <i>solely</i> as gateways to the crossover-themed Minor Spheres, at least where the Awakened are concerned.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T11:45:25-08:00","id":1504861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1504840#post1504840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5xp for the first dot, and current level times four for each dot after that. At character creation, Minor Spheres cost four freebie points per dot. However, there's also the restriction that before you can buy that first dot, you must first put two dots into the \u201cadjacent Major Spheres\u201d.<br /> <br /> <b>Foreign Magicks</b>, another STV supplement that features Minors Spheres (for crossover purposes), replaces this requirement with the requirement to take an appropriate Merit first: the Ghoul Merit gives you access to the Minor Spheres of Blood, Immortality, and Dominance; the Kinfolk Merit gives you access to the Minor Spheres of Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm; the Medium Merit gives access to the Minor Spheres of Necromancy, Oblivion, and Passion; and the Kinain Merit gives access to the Minor Spheres of Dreams, Names, and Oaths.<br /> <br /> (<b>Foreign Magicks</b> takes as its premise the idea that an Awakened Ghoul, for example, gets these Minor Spheres <i>instead of </i>developing Disciplines, and that a Kinain mage uses Dreams to perceive chimera instead of that being an innate benefit of the Kinain Merit. In short, these Merits are reimagined <i>solely</i> as gateways to the crossover-themed Minor Spheres, at least where the Awakened are concerned.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Many thanks. I find all of this highly interesting. <br /> In particular I want to use minor Spheres to fill some gaps for dark ages mage. <br /> I know that in that game mages are not supposed to be doing everything with the same kind of ease, but some spaces do need filling in my opinion <br /> <br /> In essence a minor sphere, as I understand it, could be seen as, say, a sorcerer path albeit with the pros and cons of true Magick?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T12:27:03-08:00","id":1504864,"title":"","content":"Did I mention that the Pillars are broader than the Spheres? Again, a Hermetic can do stuff that would be covered by the Spirit Sphere using conjunctions of Primus and Corona. So before you say that there are holes, let's make sure that there actually <i>are</i> holes.<br /> <br /> As well, there's precedent for there being more than four Pillars to a Foundation: the Craftmasons are presented as a splinter of the Order of Hermes, using the same Foundation and three of the same Pillars, but replacing Primus with Materia. It's also mentioned that there are some Hermetic Houses that might do likewise (I think House Verditius was pointed out as one). So there shouldn't be too much of a problem to add a \u201cfifth Pillar\u201d to other Fellowships to catch things that aren't covered by conjunctions or higher rankings of the existing Pillars. <br /> <br /> Minor Spheres operate on the assumption that there's nothing that the Major Spheres can't do, and therefore that everything that a Minor Sphere covers will be a subset of what Major Spheres cover, either individually or in conjunction. I'd expect the same to apply to Pillars and \u201cminor Pillars\u201d: they're not the right tool to \u201cfill the holes\u201d in what the \u201cmajor Pillars\u201d (don't) cover. Conjunctional uses of existing Pillars, or a \u201cfifth Pillar\u201d, would be the right tools to use. <br /> <br /> And no, Minor Spheres aren't Paths, either. The only thing they have in common with Paths is that they're not as broad as Major Spheres. Heck, they're not even using the same organizational structure: Spheres (both Major and Minor, and also Pillars) are each defined by a subject matter: a thing that the Sphere governs; by contrast, Paths are defined primarily by what they <i>do, </i>with the issue of what they affect being an implicit consequence of that. In short, Spheres and Pillars are Noun-based; Paths are Verb-based. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T16:20:59-08:00","id":1504884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1504864#post1504864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I mention that the Pillars are broader than the Spheres? Again, a Hermetic can do stuff that would be covered by the Spirit Sphere using conjunctions of Primus and Corona. So before you say that there are holes, let's make sure that there actually <i>are</i> holes.<br /> <br /> As well, there's precedent for there being more than four Pillars to a Foundation: the Craftmasons are presented as a splinter of the Order of Hermes, using the same Foundation and three of the same Pillars, but replacing Primus with Materia. It's also mentioned that there are some Hermetic Houses that might do likewise (I think House Verditius was pointed out as one). So there shouldn't be too much of a problem to add a \u201cfifth Pillar\u201d to other Fellowships to catch things that aren't covered by conjunctions or higher rankings of the existing Pillars.<br /> <br /> Minor Spheres operate on the assumption that there's nothing that the Major Spheres can't do, and therefore that everything that a Minor Sphere covers will be a subset of what Major Spheres cover, either individually or in conjunction. I'd expect the same to apply to Pillars and \u201cminor Pillars\u201d: they're not the right tool to \u201cfill the holes\u201d in what the \u201cmajor Pillars\u201d (don't) cover. Conjunctional uses of existing Pillars, or a \u201cfifth Pillar\u201d, would be the right tools to use.<br /> <br /> And no, Minor Spheres aren't Paths, either. The only thing they have in common with Paths is that they're not as broad as Major Spheres. Heck, they're not even using the same organizational structure: Spheres (both Major and Minor, and also Pillars) are each defined by a subject matter: a thing that the Sphere governs; by contrast, Paths are defined primarily by what they <i>do, </i>with the issue of what they affect being an implicit consequence of that. In short, Spheres and Pillars are Noun-based; Paths are Verb-based. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, don't worry I am well aware that primus is not just prime or that corona is not just mind etc. Anyway I will buy the books in question and figure it out myself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T04:55:01-07:00","id":1505308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1504840#post1504840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5xp for the first dot, and current level times four for each dot after that. At character creation, Minor Spheres cost four freebie points per dot. However, there's also the restriction that before you can buy that first dot, you must first put two dots into the \u201cadjacent Major Spheres\u201d.<br /> <br /> <b>Foreign Magicks</b>, another STV supplement that features Minors Spheres (for crossover purposes), replaces this requirement with the requirement to take an appropriate Merit first: the Ghoul Merit gives you access to the Minor Spheres of Blood, Immortality, and Dominance; the Kinfolk Merit gives you access to the Minor Spheres of Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm; the Medium Merit gives access to the Minor Spheres of Necromancy, Oblivion, and Passion; and the Kinain Merit gives access to the Minor Spheres of Dreams, Names, and Oaths.<br /> <br /> (<b>Foreign Magicks</b> takes as its premise the idea that an Awakened Ghoul, for example, gets these Minor Spheres <i>instead of </i>developing Disciplines, and that a Kinain mage uses Dreams to perceive chimera instead of that being an innate benefit of the Kinain Merit. In short, these Merits are reimagined <i>solely</i> as gateways to the crossover-themed Minor Spheres, at least where the Awakened are concerned.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It is nice and interesting that Ghouls becoming Mages and developing Magck Effects is mentioned. Is it outlined whether this is meant for a normal Ghoul (or a Ghoul Mage) who could be for example an important NPC, or a player character ?<br /> Also, is the other possibility in regard to this discussed - supernatural persons who were Mages and choose to try to become friends (or lovers, or allies) with particular Vampires while becoming a Ghoul ?<br /> <br /> Is it just three of these special Minor Spheres for each these type of supernatural persons ? It is certainlyl nice that Minor Sphere of Passion and Minor Sphere of Dreams are included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T08:50:17-07:00","id":1505315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1501135#post1501135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...and I bought the STV supplement about them right away...</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a moment to share your thoughts on this supplement? I love minor spheres so would be interested in something that developed them more, if it was done well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T09:28:22-07:00","id":1505319,"title":"","content":"The idea is that having an Awakened Avatar is incompatible with the powers of the Night Folk; so Awakened ghouls don't get access to vampire powers the way that Sleeper ghouls do, in much the same way that Awakened mages don't get access to sorcery the way that Sleepers do: if you're a ghoul and you Awaken, the ghoulish powers you used to have go away and get replaced by access to <b>Vampire</b>-themed Minor Spheres. And if you're Awakened and get ghouled, you don't get a Blood pool or develop Disciplines; you gain access to the ghoul-related Minor Spheres. That; and if you use the Minor Spheres in question in a way that's compatible with how the powers of the Night Folk in question normally work, you get the Coincidental edge; you basically get to treat the metaphysics of their gameline as a kind of mythic thread. <br /> <br /> The book is dealing exclusively with the Minor Spheres in question, and doesn't get into non-Awakened ghouls, kinfolk, mediums, or kinain <i>at all</i>, other than to note that they exist; its aim is to provide <b>Mage</b>-based solutions to crossover issues in the form of showing how the other games' themes .can be encapsulated in Minor Spheres instead of having one character use a blend of game systems from two separate gamelines. <br /> <br /> And yes, each type of Night Folk has three Minor Spheres associated with it, built around the other gameline's themes: ghouls have Blood, Immortality, and Dominance; kinfolk have Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm; mediums have Necromancy, Oblivion, and Passion; and kinain have Dreams, Names, and Oaths. <br /> <br /> But while the book is written with crossovers in mind, the Minor Spheres in it are written broadly enough that I could see several of them being adopted by various Traditions or other factions in <b>Mage</b> even <i>without</i> crossovers involved: Blood, for instance; while it was written from <b>Vampire</b>'s perspective, it's written in such a way that I could see the Verbenae studying it. Dominance is something that the more oppressive Technocrats might study. Passion is something I could see the Cult of Ecstasy getting into, and Names and Oaths are something I could see the Order of Hermes having an interest in. I personally think that there's more to the Euthanatoi than death; but Necromancy certainly falls within their wheelhouse.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't expect mages who access these Spheres <i>without</i> the \u201ccrossover Merits\u201d to get the aforementioned Coincidental edge; and they'd have to invest a couple of dots in the associated Major Spheres. But with those caveats in mind, I see no reason why the Minor Spheres from <b>Foreign Magicks</b> couldn't be used freely by mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T10:12:12-07:00","id":1505321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1505315#post1505315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have a moment to share your thoughts on this supplement? I love minor spheres so would be interested in something that developed them more, if it was done well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's done well. <b>Book of Fragments</b> has three chapters: <br /> <br /> The first chapter has three main sections to it: Sphere Theory, which discusses what the Major Spheres are, and what the Minor Spheres are, and <i>aren't</i> (in particular, it explains how they aren't Pillars, Paths, or cheat codes); Mechanics, which discusses the game rules for purchasing and using Minor Spheres; and Narrative, which deals with the less crunchy aspects of using Minor Spheres in the game. <br /> The second chapter covers nine Minor Spheres: Desire (which I could see being used both by Cultists of Ecstasy and by the Syndicate), Emergence (a Sphere that acts in some ways as an inversion of Entropy's destructive aspects; it's about order emerging from chaos), Fire (House Flambeau would love this; but the Children of Knowledge also embrace it as the Sphere of Multiplicatio), Glory (the Chorus <i>loves</i> this one; it's ideally suited to \u201cmiracle workers\u201d), Harmony (this would be to the Akashayana as Glory is to the Choristers), Hearth (Magick dealing with the home), Meaning (highly compatible with the \u201creality as simulation\u201d Paradigm), Metamorphosis (the Sphere of shapechanging, in all its myriad forms), and Night (for those mages who view darkness as a thing unto itself, not merely an absence of light). <br /> <br /> The third chapter has sections on how to create your own Minor Spheres (in a nutshell: pick four Major Spheres and a Concept; the Minor Sphere can do anything that the selected Major Spheres can, individually or in conjunction, but only as they relate to the Concept) and on how to incorporate them into your game (this gets into tweaking the rules for Minor Spheres in case the ones thus far given don't do what you want them to). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T09:49:48-07:00","id":1505438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1505321#post1505321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's done well. <b>Book of Fragments</b> has three chapters:<br /> <br /> The first chapter has three main sections to it: Sphere Theory, which discusses what the Major Spheres are, and what the Minor Spheres are, and <i>aren't</i> (in particular, it explains how they aren't Pillars, Paths, or cheat codes); Mechanics, which discusses the game rules for purchasing and using Minor Spheres; and Narrative, which deals with the less crunchy aspects of using Minor Spheres in the game.<br /> The second chapter covers nine Minor Spheres: Desire (which I could see being used both by Cultists of Ecstasy and by the Syndicate), Emergence (a Sphere that acts in some ways as an inversion of Entropy's destructive aspects; it's about order emerging from chaos), Fire (House Flambeau would love this; but the Children of Knowledge also embrace it as the Sphere of Multiplicatio), Glory (the Chorus <i>loves</i> this one; it's ideally suited to \u201cmiracle workers\u201d), Harmony (this would be to the Akashayana as Glory is to the Choristers), Hearth (Magick dealing with the home), Meaning (highly compatible with the \u201creality as simulation\u201d Paradigm), Metamorphosis (the Sphere of shapechanging, in all its myriad forms), and Night (for those mages who view darkness as a thing unto itself, not merely an absence of light).<br /> <br /> The third chapter has sections on how to create your own Minor Spheres (in a nutshell: pick four Major Spheres and a Concept; the Minor Sphere can do anything that the selected Major Spheres can, individually or in conjunction, but only as they relate to the Concept) and on how to incorporate them into your game (this gets into tweaking the rules for Minor Spheres in case the ones thus far given don't do what you want them to).</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent, thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T12:54:26-07:00","id":1505496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501067-did-victorian-mage-use-minor-spheres?p=1505321#post1505321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's done well. <b>Book of Fragments</b> has three chapters:<br /> <br /> The first chapter has three main sections to it: Sphere Theory, which discusses what the Major Spheres are, and what the Minor Spheres are, and <i>aren't</i> (in particular, it explains how they aren't Pillars, Paths, or cheat codes); Mechanics, which discusses the game rules for purchasing and using Minor Spheres; and Narrative, which deals with the less crunchy aspects of using Minor Spheres in the game.<br /> The second chapter covers nine Minor Spheres: Desire (which I could see being used both by Cultists of Ecstasy and by the Syndicate), Emergence (a Sphere that acts in some ways as an inversion of Entropy's destructive aspects; it's about order emerging from chaos), Fire (House Flambeau would love this; but the Children of Knowledge also embrace it as the Sphere of Multiplicatio), Glory (the Chorus <i>loves</i> this one; it's ideally suited to \u201cmiracle workers\u201d), Harmony (this would be to the Akashayana as Glory is to the Choristers), Hearth (Magick dealing with the home), Meaning (highly compatible with the \u201creality as simulation\u201d Paradigm), Metamorphosis (the Sphere of shapechanging, in all its myriad forms), and Night (for those mages who view darkness as a thing unto itself, not merely an absence of light).<br /> <br /> The third chapter has sections on how to create your own Minor Spheres (in a nutshell: pick four Major Spheres and a Concept; the Minor Sphere can do anything that the selected Major Spheres can, individually or in conjunction, but only as they relate to the Concept) and on how to incorporate them into your game (this gets into tweaking the rules for Minor Spheres in case the ones thus far given don't do what you want them to).</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds very good, intricate, nice, and interesting. Minor Spheres of elements and forces like frost or light would be a nice addition. As would Minor Spheres created around concepts like conflict, betrayal, or prosperity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}